From 06e0ee6e7e060475d1cdbee9b26384b717fb4d9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:14:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 73/77] test: add feature_p2mr_slhdsa128s.py

On regtest, with the rules from height 200, a node with the default
policy and one with -acceptnonstdtxn=1, and a missing P2MR tripwire
output that disables elliptic curve checks in leaf version 0xe0 from
height 150:

- the startup log, getdeploymentinfo, and -signetslhdsa128s refused on
  regtest;
- the mempool refuses a valid SLH1 spend while the next block is below
  the height, on both nodes, and takes it from the block before; a block
  below the height takes invalid signatures in leaf versions 0xc0 and
  0xe0; the first block at the height, built on the block below it, is
  rejected for an invalid signature in either leaf version with the tip
  unchanged, and then a valid block at the height confirms valid spends
  in both; a later block rejects an invalid signature too;
- a reorganization below the height removes the SLH-DSA spends of both
  mempools, the template one and a non-template one, with their
  children;
- after activation, SLH1 with hash type 0x83 and in leaf version 0xe0,
  whose elliptic curve checks are disabled, relays and confirms; each of
  the four new script errors is refused in the mempool and in a block;
- checks whose budget is used up exactly pass in a block, one unit short
  fail; their number and the padding follow from the validation weight;
- policy: non-template leaves, a leaf at depth zero, an extra stack
  element;
- a leaf with an ML-DSA-44 and an SLH-DSA check, and a transaction with
  P2MR SLH-DSA, ML-DSA-44 and Schnorr inputs and a P2TR input.

It makes ten SLH-DSA signatures in Python and derives the invalid
witnesses from them.
